 :references
 {:buckley2017 {:cite "Buckley, C. L., Kim, C. S., McGregor, S., & Seth, A. K. (2017). The free energy principle for action and perception: a mathematical review. Journal of Mathematical Psychology, 81, 55-79."
                :used-for "continuous (Laplace) free energy as precision-weighted squared prediction error; belief update by gradient descent on F"
                :verified {:eq9 "general variational free energy F" :eq45 "Laplace-encoded energy: sum over channels of ½ ε²/σ + ½ ln σ" :eq58 "instance for the worked model" :eq59 "recognition dynamics (gradient descent on the energy)"
                           :eq77 "multivariate Laplace-encoded energy as precision-weighted sum of squared errors (per C453)" :eq78-79 "prediction errors (per C453)" :eq84 "precision as inverse variance (per C453)" :eq48-50 "recognition dynamics as gradient descent (per C453)" :eq82-86 "precision-weighted errors (per C453)"}
                :local-specialisations "The registry's channel forms -- ε_k := o_k − μ_k, Π_k := 1/max(Var_k, ε₀), F = ½ mean_k Π_k ε_k², μ ← μ + αΠε -- are NOT written in this paper (C453). They are stack specialisations of eqs. 45/77-79/84/59: single channel per error, sample variance with a floor, mean over channels, one fixed-step update."
                :retrieved "refs/buckley2017.pdf"}
  :dacosta2020 {:cite "Da Costa, L., Parr, T., Sajid, N., Veselic, S., Neacsu, V., & Friston, K. (2020). Active inference on discrete state-spaces: a synthesis. Journal of Mathematical Psychology, 99, 102447."
                :used-for "expected free energy G = ambiguity + risk (- novelty); policy posterior softmax over -G; action as argmax; Dirichlet parameter learning; deep temporal models"
                :verified {:eq42 "G(π) = E_Q(s|π)[H[P(o|s)]] + D_KL[Q(s|π)||P(s)] - novelty (Appendix C)" :eq44 "risk over outcomes: (A s)·(log(A s) - log C), the form used when preferences are over outcomes" :eq45-48 "ambiguity = H · s_π, H := -diag[A·log A]" :eq10 "Q(π) = σ(-G(π)) -- omits E and temperature; footnote 5 gives the fuller σ(−ln E − F − G) per C453 (sign of the E term as transcribed there); A.2 adds γ separately" :eq11 "u_t = argmax_u Σ_π δ_{u,π_t} Q(π)" :eq21 "a = a + Σ_τ o_τ ⊗ s_τ" :eq38 "Q(π) = σ(-G(π; β)), β ≥ 0" :A2 "γ as inverse temperature: σ(-γ G(π))" :A4 "deep temporal (hierarchical) models"}
                :retrieved "refs/dacosta2020.pdf"}
  :friston2017 {:cite "Friston, K., FitzGerald, T., Rigoli, F., Schwartenbeck, P., & Pezzulo, G. (2017). Active inference: a process theory. Neural Computation, 29(1), 1-49."
                :used-for "the perception-evaluation-selection-action loop as a process; precision γ of policy selection and its β update"
                :verified {:eq2.1 "P(π) = σ(-γ · G(π))" :eq2.7 "belief-update set: s = σ(A·o + B s_{τ-1} + B·s_{τ+1}); π = σ(-F - γ·G); β = β + (π - π₀)·G; γ = 1/β"}
                :note "The habit prior E does NOT appear in this paper; see :friston2016."
                :retrieved "refs/friston2017.pdf"}
  :parr2022 {:cite "Parr, T., Pezzulo, G., & Friston, K. J. (2022). Active Inference: The Free Energy Principle in Mind, Brain, and Behavior. MIT Press."
             :used-for "consolidated discrete notation; THE source that writes the policy posterior with the habit term: π = σ(ln E − F − G)"
             :verified {:eq4.7 "policy prior and expected free energy (ch. 4, pp. 72-74; per C453)" :eq4.9 "risk/ambiguity and information-gain/pragmatic forms (per C453)" :eq4.10 "linear-algebra form with A, C, softmax (per C453)" :eqB.7 "P(π) = Cat(π₀), p. 246" :eqB.8 "F = π · (ln π − ln E + F + G), p. 247" :eqB.9 "π = σ(ln E − F − G), p. 247 -- read from the retrieved PDF by claude-1"}
             :retrieved "refs/parr2022.pdf (mirror located by wm-evidence, C453)"}
  :friston2016 {:cite "Friston, K., FitzGerald, T., Rigoli, F., Schwartenbeck, P., O'Doherty, J., & Pezzulo, G. (2016). Active inference and learning. Neuroscience and Biobehavioral Reviews, 68, 862-879."
                :used-for "the habit prior E over policies, learned as Dirichlet concentration parameters over policies"
                :verified {:eq6 "referenced at §5.3, p. 874: 'this prior probability is based upon the policy concentration parameters, e ⊂ η (see Eq. (6))' -- verified by eye from the rendered page"}
                :retrieved "refs/friston2016.pdf"}
  :friston2018bmr {:cite "Friston, K., Parr, T., & Zeidman, P. (2018). Bayesian model reduction. arXiv:1805.07092."
                   :used-for "Bayesian model reduction: evidence change for a reduced model, used by structure learning"
                   :verified {:eq9 "F[P̃:P] = ln E_Q[P̃(θ)/P(θ)] + F[P]: log evidence of the reduced model" :table1 "closed forms; Dirichlet row" :text "p. 617 region: a reduced model is accepted when its log-evidence gain is greater than zero (the paper's ΔF is reduced minus full)"}
                   :sign-convention "The War Machine's ΔF (Holes.lean modelReductionFreeEnergyChange; bmr.clj) is ln B(A) + ln B(a′) − ln B(a) − ln B(A′), which is the NEGATIVE of the paper's reduced-minus-full log evidence, i.e. ΔF_WM = ln P(y|full) − ln P(y|reduced). Verified numerically 2026-09-01: identical rows give ΔF_WM = −5.01, paper +5.01. Hence 'accept when ΔF_WM ≤ −3' means the reduced model wins by ≥ 3 nats."
                   :retrieved "refs/friston2018bmr.pdf"}
  :kass1995 {:cite "Kass, R. E., & Raftery, A. E. (1995). Bayes factors. Journal of the American Statistical Association, 90(430), 773-795."
             :used-for "the log-evidence threshold of 3 ('strong') behind bayesFactorThreshold"
             :verified {:table2 "p. 777: 2 ln B₁₀ in 6–10 (B₁₀ 20–150) = 'strong'; > 10 = 'very strong'. So ln BF ≥ 3 is the lower edge of 'strong'. Verified by eye (scanned PDF)."}
             :note "Supports the magnitude 3 only; the direction is the WM sign convention stated under :friston2018bmr."
             :retrieved "refs/kass1995.pdf"}}

 ;; Exogenous symbols: imported by equations, defined by no equation here.
 ;; :class :stack-defined means the War Machine supplies the content.
 :exogenous
 [{:symbol :A :meaning "observation model P(o|s)" :class :stack-defined :glossary "Observation model A" :node :R4}
  {:symbol :B :meaning "transition model P(s'|s,pi)" :class :stack-defined :glossary "Generative model" :node :R4}
  {:symbol :C :meaning "preference distribution over outcomes" :class :stack-defined :glossary "Preferences (R19 stack)" :node nil
   :note "C has no node in control-stages.edn; it lives in the R19 preference stack registry"}
  {:symbol :E :meaning "habit prior over policies" :class :stack-defined :glossary "Softmax and controller calibration" :node :R6}
  {:symbol :alpha :meaning "belief-update step size" :class :stack-defined :glossary "Prediction error" :node :R3}
  {:symbol :eps0 :meaning "variance floor in the precision map" :class :stack-defined :glossary "Precision" :node :R7}
  {:symbol :world :meaning "the environment: actuation changes what is next observed" :class :external :node :R16}]

 ;; Equations. :imports lists symbols; each is defined by another row's
 ;; :defines or listed under :exogenous. :node is the R-box that runs it.
 :equations
 [{:id :observe :defines :o :node :R2 :class :stack-defined :ref :friston2017
   :imports [:world]
   :formal "o_t <- structured observation of the world after action u_{t-1}"}
  {:id :prediction-error :defines :eps :node :R8 :class :theory-defined :ref :buckley2017
   :imports [:o :mu]
   :formal "eps_k := o_k - mu_k" :eq "buckley2017 eq. 45 error terms (reduction: no generalised coordinates)" :lean nil :lean-status :missing
   :code "war_machine.clj:4368-4379"}
  {:id :precision :defines :Pi :node :R7 :class :theory-defined :ref :buckley2017
   :imports [:eps :eps0]
   :formal "Pi_k := 1 / max(Var(eps_k), eps0)" :eq nil :lean nil :lean-status :missing
   :note "Var(eps_k) is the bounded rolling variance of channel k's prediction ERROR history (precision.clj:116-135 update-channel-precision: production precision is the variance component of new-error; the observation enters only the separately emitted :salience term under the default :salience-mode :separate). Earlier this row imported :o and said 'variance of o_k' -- corrected 2026-09-01 (C10, found reviewing D5f): at symbol grain R7 imports eps, so the theory edge is R8->R7, and R2->R7 holds only at route grain. In buckley2017 eq. 45 the variances σ are model parameters, not sample statistics; this row is therefore stack-defined in content and only theory-defined in role." :code "precision.clj:116-135, 160-190; war_machine.clj:4380-4388"}
  {:id :free-energy :defines :F :node :R8 :class :theory-defined :ref :buckley2017
   :imports [:Pi :eps]
   :formal "F = 1/2 * mean_k (Pi_k eps_k^2)" :eq "buckley2017 eq. 45 (reduction: ½ ln σ terms dropped; mean over channels instead of sum)" :lean "variationalFreeEnergy" :lean-status :closed
   :code "free_energy.clj:184-205; war_machine.clj:4450-4452"
   :live-consumer nil :status :shortcut-to-retire :note "Computed and stored each tick; NO live consumer reads it (C448 5c.1). Joe's ruling 2026-09-01 (J2, :choices :free-energy-form): a shortcut to retire, not a diagnostic to keep."}
  {:id :belief-update :defines :mu-next :node :R3 :class :theory-defined :ref :buckley2017
   :imports [:mu :Pi :eps :alpha]
   :formal "mu <- mu + alpha Pi eps" :eq "buckley2017 eq. 59 (reduction: one gradient step with fixed step size alpha)" :lean nil :lean-status :missing
   :code "war_machine.clj:4375-4388, 4429-4431"}
  {:id :belief-state :defines :mu :node :R1 :class :stack-defined :ref :buckley2017
   :imports [:mu-next]
   :formal "mu_t := the stored belief after the update at t-1"}
  {:id :forward-model :defines :Q-o-pi :node :R4 :class :theory-defined :ref :dacosta2020
   :imports [:mu :A :B :pi :T]
   :formal "Q(o|pi) := sum_s A(o|s) Q(s|pi), Q(s|pi) rolled forward by B from mu over depth T" :eq "dacosta2020 eq. 42-44 (the predictive terms A s_π)" :code "efe.clj:601-609; forward_model.clj:279-324"
   :lean "PredictiveOutcomeKernel" :lean-status :carrier-only
   :note "Q-interface-completeness.edn records 2 missing wires for this row"}
  {:id :risk :defines :risk :node :R5 :class :theory-defined :ref :dacosta2020
   :imports [:Q-o-pi :C]
   :formal "risk(pi) := D_KL[Q(o|pi) || C]" :eq "dacosta2020 eq. 44 (risk over outcomes)" :lean "predictiveOutcomeRisk" :lean-status :closed}
  {:id :ambiguity :defines :ambiguity :node :R5 :class :theory-defined :ref :dacosta2020
   :imports [:Q-o-pi :A]
   :formal "ambiguity(pi) := E_{Q(s|pi)}[H(P(o|s))]" :eq "dacosta2020 eq. 45-48" :lean "ambiguity" :lean-status :closed}
  {:id :expected-free-energy :defines :G :node :R5 :class :theory-defined :ref :dacosta2020
   :imports [:risk :ambiguity]
   :formal "G(pi) := risk(pi) + ambiguity(pi)" :eq "dacosta2020 eq. 42 WITHOUT the novelty term -E[D_KL[Q(A|o,s)||Q(A)]]" :lean "expectedFreeEnergy" :lean-status :closed
   :omits "novelty (parameter-exploration) term of eq. 42; the WM has no Dirichlet Q(A) live, so the term is identically absent rather than approximated"
   :conflict "Holes.G := risk - eig over a generic Policy; G_eq_expectedFreeEnergy bridges the two under stated assumptions (glossary-formal-lines.md, G entry)"}
  {:id :policy-set :defines :pi :node :R6 :class :stack-defined :ref :friston2017
   :imports []
   :formal "pi ranges over the candidate action space"}
  {:id :depth :defines :T :node :R13 :class :theory-defined :ref :dacosta2020
   :imports []
   :formal "T := temporal policy depth (the range of the sums in Q(o|pi) and G)" :eq "dacosta2020 eq. 42 (sum over τ)" :code "war_machine.clj:4485-4487 (3 when an anticipation snapshot loads); rollout.clj:166-171 (default 2)"}
  {:id :temperature :defines :tau :node :R14 :class :stack-defined :ref :friston2017
   :imports []
   :formal "tau := commitment temperature (inverse precision gamma of policy selection)" :eq "friston2017 eq. 2.1 (γ = 1/β); dacosta2020 A.2" :code "policy.clj:242-245 (effective-temperature from selection gain / score spread)"}
  {:id :policy-posterior :defines :Q-pi :node :R6 :class :theory-defined :ref :parr2022 :also-refs [:dacosta2020 :friston2017 :friston2016]
   :imports [:E :G :tau :pi]
   :formal "Q(pi) := softmax(ln E(pi) - G(pi)/tau)" :eq "parr2022 eq. B.9 (π = σ(ln E − F − G), p. 247) with γ = 1/τ from friston2017 eq. 2.1 / dacosta2020 A.2; the registry form drops F_π (the WM scores policies by G only) -- a stack specialisation. E's meaning: friston2016 eq. 6 (habit as policy concentration parameters)" :lean "softmax" :lean-status :closed
   :code "policy.clj:242-245, 411-438" :note "Computed and recorded; the live path then selects deterministically (see :action)."}
  {:id :action :defines :u :node :R16 :class :theory-defined :ref :friston2017
   :imports [:Q-pi]
   :formal "u_t := argmax_u sum_pi delta(u, pi_t) Q(pi)" :eq "dacosta2020 eq. 11 (Bayesian-model-average argmax); friston2017 eq. 2.3 selects the action minimising expected outcome prediction error -- two deterministic rules in the literature, neither is sampling (C453)"
   :code "policy.clj:247-250 (first admissible controller entry), :411-438 (max-key)" :note "The code's deterministic selection conforms to eq. 11. C448 5b: the enacted action at R16 is the first passing act gate (enact.clj:287-316), not the recorded selection -- see :holes."}
  {:id :dirichlet-accumulation :defines :a-conc :node :R17 :class :theory-defined :ref :dacosta2020
   :imports [:o :mu]
   :formal "a = a + sum_tau o_tau (x) s_tau  (Dirichlet concentrations accumulated from observed outcome/state pairs)" :eq "dacosta2020 eq. 21 (A-learning; B/D learning A.1 eqs. 27-33 per C453)"
   :lean "DirichletConcentrations (carrier only, Holes.lean:6380-6385)" :lean-status :carrier-only
   :realised false
   :code "NOT realised. What a4a accumulates is a different model: corpus->concentration (a4a.clj:85-113) counts capability x mission edge/discharge pairs over a uniform 0.1 prior, fed only by a4a-substrate/read-corpus (a4a_substrate.clj:46-60), which reads capability entities, mission docs, :capability/* hyperedges and discharges from the SUBSTRATE over Drawbridge. No trace mention in a4a.clj, a4a_substrate.clj or r17_offline.clj. The substrate's :capability/* hyperedges and :discharge entities are written by the A3 actuator (actuator_a3.clj:31, :68, :486-487), and a4a.clj:2-6 states that concepts are 'demo-validated until real :capability/* production writes flow' -- i.e. the feeder exists but production writes do not yet (claude-20 check, C456; claude-1 re-check, 2026-09-01)."
   :note "The theory edges R2->R17 and R1->R17 (o and μ into the Dirichlet accumulation, eq. 21) have no realisation found. An earlier version of this row claimed realisation 'by way of TRACE'; that was wrong (registry author's error, corrected on claude-20's check). The BMR the WM runs is over a capability x mission Dirichlet model built from substrate graph structure, not over the tick model's o and μ."}
  {:id :model-reduction :defines :Delta-F :node :R17 :class :theory-defined :ref :friston2018bmr
   :imports [:a-conc]  ;; C453: BMR takes the full posterior and full/reduced priors (Dirichlet concentrations), not the scalar F. Earlier [:F] was the registry author's error.
   :formal "Delta F := ln P(y|full) - ln P(y|reduced) = ln B(A) + ln B(a') - ln B(a) - ln B(A') over Dirichlet concentrations a (prior), A (posterior), a' (reduced prior); a reduction is accepted when Delta F <= -3" :eq "friston2018bmr eq. 9 and Table 1 (Dirichlet), sign reversed: see :references :friston2018bmr :sign-convention"
   :code "bmr.clj:108-130; a4a.clj:126-159 (offline)" :note "No live consumer of per-tick F feeds this; R17 runs offline (r17_offline.clj)."
   :lean "bayesFactorThreshold" :lean-status :closed :threshold-ref :kass1995}]

 ;; Where the framework leaves a free hand. Each is recorded as OBSERVED in
 ;; the War Machine as of 2026-09-01; Joe decides. Format mirrors
 ;; control-map-edges.edn :decisions so a decision can replace an observation.
 :choices
 {:free-energy-form {:observed :laplace-channel-grain-diagnostic :status :decided
                     :ruling {:by "joe" :at "2026-09-01" :grounds :ruling
                              :decision "The current Laplace channel F is a shortcut (J2). Do not accept it as a diagnostic to keep: retire it, and replace it with theory-aligned free-energy quantities that are actually needed and consumed -- the per-policy F_pi that the policy posterior imports (parr2022 eq. B.9: pi = sigma(ln E - F - G)), and a belief update that is the gradient of the F the machine reports, at one grain."
                              :consequence "The F row (R8) is marked :status :shortcut-to-retire; it stays in the registry and the figure until its replacement is realised and consumed, so the drawing keeps matching the code. Opened H4 (hole: F_pi not computed, F not consumed) and I2 (implement F_pi into Q(pi)) in worklist.edn."}
                     :evidence "free_energy.clj:184-205; war_machine.clj:4450-4452; efe.clj:601-619, 782-794 (C448 5c.1)"
                     :statement "F is the continuous Laplace form over error channels and has no live consumer; the policy side is the discrete formulation (dacosta2020). No retrieved source cites this mixed-grain composition as one formalism; it is a stack composition unless a source is found."}
  :temperature-update {:observed :selection-gain-fold-default :status :decided
                       :ruling {:by "joe" :at "2026-09-01" :grounds :ruling
                                :decision "The current tau -- from selection gain / score spread -- is a shortcut, and the drawn R7->R14 was a conflation of two precision-like scalars (J1: no). Pursue the theory-aligned policy precision: gamma = 1/beta with beta updated from the policies' expected free energy (friston2017 eq. 2.7, over the gamma prior P(gamma) = Gamma(1, beta) of eq. 2.1), so that the machine's decisiveness is the formalism's, not an engineering proxy."
                                :sources-note "C461 §6 (2026-09-01) corrected two citations claude-1 wrote into the I1 packet: dacosta2020 A.2 supports only gamma's ROLE in selection (sigma(-G) 'can be extended to sigma(-gamma G)', referring to [44] for the update scheme) and is not a source for the beta update; and in eq. 2.7 pi0 = sigma(-gamma . G), the EFE-only distribution (friston2017.txt:684), not the habit prior E. Eq. 2.7's F is the per-policy F_pi (notation table, friston2017.txt:291) -- the same object as parr2022 B.4 -- so the beta update depends on I2's F_pi (J3). Second read (claude-20, 2026-09-01): dropping dacosta2020 A.2 is right, but dropping eq. 2.1 with it over-corrected -- 2.1 is where beta is introduced, as the rate of the gamma prior P(gamma) = Gamma(1, beta) (friston2017.txt:325-336); 2.7 gives the update, 2.1 gives the prior it is over, so both belong. Also note for anyone diffing this file against a generated figure: the :decision string above, stamped :by joe, was AMENDED after Joe ruled -- its citation list was claude-1's summary wording, not Joe's, and the amendment is C13 plus this second read. Joe's ruling itself (J1: no) is unchanged."
                                :consequence "D4's retirement of R7->R14 stands; no ruling-added edge. Opened H3 (hole: gamma is not the theory's) and I1 (implement beta/gamma dynamics) in worklist.edn."}
                       :evidence "war_machine.clj:238-248 (default :selection-gain-only; FUTON_WM_TAU_MODE selects score-spread); selection_gain.clj:173-206 folds realised outcomes; policy.clj:32-80 (C448 5c.2)"
                       :theory-alternative "friston2017 eq. 2.7: β = β + (π - π₀)·G, γ = 1/β -- not implemented"
                       :statement "The mechanism updates tau from realised selection gain (default) or score spread, not by the β/γ precision dynamics. But LIVE: the judge calls fold-realized-outcome every tick (war_machine.clj:4332-4361) and the fold returns the state unchanged unless a well-formed unseen :realized-outcome is present, and that field is absent on today's live path, simulation-only (selection_gain.clj:187-193; C454). So live tau holds at its prior: an update check runs per tick and never fires. 'Fixed-calibrated' described the live behaviour; 'folds realised outcomes' describes the mechanism; both are needed."}
  :habit-prior {:observed :implemented-not-applied-live :status :observed-not-decided
                :evidence "habit_prior.clj:70-89, 100-163 (learned, persisted); war_machine.clj:262-271, 4276-4283; policy.clj:234-271 (:habit-prior-applied? false on the live path) (C448 5c.3)"
                :statement "E is learned and persisted but the live strategic path does not apply it; the two run records carry no habit state."}
  :gamma-fixed-point
  {:status :decided
   :statement "TWO questions, and the source settles the first. WITHIN A TICK: pi = sigma(-F - gamma.G) and the beta update are mutually dependent -- gamma needs pi, and the policy posterior that defines pi imports tau = 1/gamma. friston2017 states the scheme outright: 'usually one would iterate the equalities in equation 2.7 until convergence' (friston2017.txt:683-685), with the gradient form in appendix B (:1690-1720) as the robust alternative. That is the formalism's answer, not an option. ACROSS TICKS: eq. 2.7 reads beta_posterior = beta_prior + (pi - pi0).G -- two distinct symbols the text extraction collapses. P(gamma) = Gamma(1, beta_prior) at :339 and Q(gamma) = Gamma(1, beta_posterior) at :357 are the prior/posterior pair, and the precision prediction error at :1711 is eps_gamma = (beta_prior - beta_posterior) + (pi - pi0).G, which would be identically zero in its first term if the two were one symbol. What the paper does NOT say is what beta_prior is at the start of each tick. That silence is the choice point."
   :options {:carried-prior "The previous tick's converged beta_posterior becomes this tick's beta_prior -- precision learned across ticks, the shape futon2.aif.selection-gain already uses (read/coerce at war_machine.clj:4332-4361, written back at :4773-4776). The machine gets more or less decisive as its policy evidence accumulates. Keeps the PERSISTENCE SHAPE of today's default path, and nothing else."
             :fixed-prior "beta_prior resets to a declared beta_0 every tick. Each tick's decisiveness is set only by this tick's G and pi; nothing about precision is remembered. Keeps the WITHIN-TICK FRESHNESS of FUTON_WM_TAU_MODE=spread, which is not the default. Simpler, and the arm against which carrying is measurable."}
   :control "TODAY'S DEFAULT LIVE PATH IS NEITHER ARM, and that is what dissolves the argument about which one it resembles (claude-1, 2026-09-01). On the default :selection-gain-only mode, tau comes from a CARRIED state that never updates live -- fold-realized-outcome's own docstring says the :realized-outcome field is absent today, sim-only (C2, C454) -- so today is a carried prior that does not move. Each arm therefore resembles today in exactly one aspect and departs in the other: :carried-prior keeps the persistence and adds the movement; :fixed-prior keeps the staticness and drops the persistence. The experiment's control must be the default live path itself, not either arm. A control chosen from the two things being compared is the failure this campaign keeps finding one level down."
   :ruling {:by "joe" :at "2026-09-01" :grounds :ruling :decision :carried-prior
            :statement "beta_prior at the start of each tick is the previous tick converged beta_posterior. beta_0 remains required as the first-tick prior and must be declared and reported, never defaulted silently."
            :implied-by-the-source "An argument from the paper structure, not a sentence in it. friston2017 splits the approximate posterior into states and parameters -- x = (s_tilde, pi, eta) with eta = (a, b, d, beta) (:343) -- so beta is a PARAMETER, in the same tuple as the Dirichlet concentrations. Of that side the paper says the updates 'accumulate coincidences over time, because parameters are time invariant (in contrast to states that change over time)' (:815). States are re-derived per tick; parameters accumulate. :fixed-prior would move a member of eta onto the state side of the paper own division. Joe reached this before the check: 'the theory should say beta is carried, as i think that is implied'."
